<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lachit Borphukan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1622–1672</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lachit Borphukan was a general of the Ahom kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>. Appointed Borphukan, commander of the western region, by King Chakradhwaj Singha, he led the recapture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guwahati">Guwahati</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> in 1667 and in 1671 won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saraighat">Battle of Saraighat</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a>. He died the following year and is honoured in Assam as a national hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lachit-borphukan.jpg" alt="Lachit Borphukan" width="268" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: বিকাশ দিহিঙ্গীয়া · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Status_of_lachit_borphhukon_and_ahom_sibsagar_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
